  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "cluster",
      "term": "Cluster",
      "definition": "Three trebles worked into the same chain-space, joined at the top. The basic building block of the granny square."
    },
    {
      "slug": "chain-space",
      "term": "Chain space",
      "definition": "The gap created by skipping a chain or chains. Corner chain-2 spaces hold the corner cluster pairs; side chain-1 spaces separate cluster pairs along the sides."
    },
    {
      "slug": "colour-change",
      "term": "Colour change",
      "definition": "In granny square work, the cleanest method is a fasten-off at the end of a round, then joining the new colour at the start of the next round with a slip stitch into a corner chain-space."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-working-in-the-round", "crochet-colour-change"],
  "criticalTechniques": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-colour-change"],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The three-colour granny square is the Victorian scrap-cotton construction that made the granny square popular in the first place. Colour A works round 1 alone, building the four corner "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pairs at the centre. Colour B picks up for rounds 2 and 3, then fastens off. Colour C finishes the outer border in round 4. Each "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "colour-change" } }],
            "text": "colour-change"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a clean break rather than a carry — each colour fastens off at its last round and the new colour joins at the corner "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the start of the next."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is the fastest way to work through a bag of small yarn remnants: each motif uses as little as 1.5 g of colour A, 3 g of colour B, and 2 g of colour C. No two squares need to match, and a blanket of random three-colour squares with a consistent outer border colour reads as intentional rather than chaotic."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 1.5 g of colour A, 3 g of colour B, and 2 g of colour C in DK-weight cotton. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished four-round three-colour granny square measures 10 × 10 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a light steam-block. When working from remnants of varying weights, check that your yarn is genuinely DK — a 4-ply colour in the centre will give a tighter, smaller centre ring."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; called double crochet (dc) in US patterns." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first cluster. Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1 — Colour A" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With colour A, form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3. Pull tail to close ring. Fasten off colour A. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2 — Colour B" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join colour B with a sl st into any ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3 — Colour B" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. Fasten off colour B. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 8 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 4 — Colour C" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join colour C with a sl st into any ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. Fasten off colour C. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 12 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring. Round 1 is colour A, rounds 2 and 3 are colour B, round 4 is colour C. Each colour change is shown as a new join at a corner chain-2 space."
          }
        ]
      },
